    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2509.23722_rag::chunk_009</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2509.23722_rag::chunk_004</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2410.07192_rag::chunk_004</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2509.23722_rag::chunk_003</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2509.24859_rag::chunk_004</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2510.15596_rag::chunk_010</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This permutation increases the effective number of pipeline stages, resulting in more fine-grained computation tasks.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the model is partitioned into multiple stages. A common strategy is to evenly allocate transformer layers across stages</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Each partition contains a set of model layers. Each partition is called a pipeline stage</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the model is divided into sequential pipeline stages, each comprising a set of consecutive layers.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The framework then enumerates all adjacent layer subsequence as candidate pipeline stages</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Each partition is called a pipeline stage .</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">8 ranks constitute one node, which is assigned to a pipeline stage.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
