    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">optimizer states dominate memory usage and scale linearly with model size</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Adam optimizer consumes 16 bytes of memory per parameter during training: 4 |{z} master weights + 4 |{z} gradients + 4 + 4 | {z } Adam states = 16 bytes</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">parameters, gradients, and optimizer states dominate memory usage</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">offload optimizer states and updates to the CPU [ 52 , 55 ], which significantly reduces GPU memory consumption</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ZeRO-1 partitions optimizer states ( OS ) across GPUs, allowing each GPU to store only one shard.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
